  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rohde and Schwarz Usa obligated $424M in FY2026 to date across 72 awards, with an average award size of $5.9M. Obligations are up 235.7% year over year. The Department of Transportation obligated $403M to Rohde and Schwarz Usa in FY2026 to date, making that agency the dominant buyer in the current fiscal year. Rohde and Schwarz Usa’s federal obligations show growth over multiple years: $20.2M in FY21, $25M in FY22, $56.2M in FY23, $35.3M in FY24, and $126M in FY25. Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing generated $403M in FY2026 to date for Rohde and Schwarz Usa. Rohde and Schwarz Usa recorded additional obligations in Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals ($8.8M) and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing ($8.4M). Rohde and Schwarz Usa also received obligations in Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing ($1.1M) and Totalizing Fluid Meter and Counting Device Manufacturing ($964K).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Rohde and Schwarz Usa’s biggest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $403M to Rohde and Schwarz Usa in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $18.6M, and the Department of Commerce obligated $1.4M. Department of Homeland Security obligated $434K, National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $251K, and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $126K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What product and industry markets drive Rohde and Schwarz Usa’s obligations?",
        "body": "Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing generated $403M in FY2026 to date for Rohde and Schwarz Usa. Instrument Manufacturing for Measuring and Testing Electricity and Electrical Signals and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $8.8M and $8.4M respectively. Rohde and Schwarz Usa also had obligations in Totalizing Fluid Meter and Counting Device Manufacturing ($964K) and Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing ($239K)."
      }
    ]
